  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implementation of a Phytosanitary Capacity Evaluation (PCE) in Nepal</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A Phytosanitary Capacity Evaluation (PCE) is conducted in Nepal, as part of a global initiative
The International Plant Protection Convention (IPPC) is an intergovernmental treaty signed by over 180 countries, aiming to protecting the world&apos;s plant resources from the spread and introduction of pests, and promoting safe trade. The Convention introduced International Standards for Phytosanitary Measures (ISPMs) as its main tool to achieve its goals, making it the sole global standard setting organization for plant health.</narrative>
  </description>
